From a8a16669a3ec7d0ec275afc0d314c046ca1e02d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:28:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer, windowing/gbm: map an HDR10+ picture by its
 HDR10+ metadata, and say what the output does with its tone curve

The decoder keeps each picture's HDR10+ metadata (VideoPicture::
hdr10PlusDynamic) as its InfoFrame is kept: fewer than 12 pictures in a row
without their own keep those of the last one, the 12th goes back to the
static metadata, and a seek keeps nothing (CMetadataHold). The renderer gives
them to the bridge where it maps the picture to the display or to SDR (CPU and
VAAPI pictures), not where it draws the picture as it is.

kodi.log says, once a video, what happens to the tone curve and the targeted
display of a video's HDR10+ metadata: mapped by it (the bridge's note says
how: the target, the knee point, the anchors, the display's peak and, where
that is not the target, that libplacebo adapts the curve), refused and why,
not carried as Dolby Vision (level 1 comes from the HDR10+ statistics), sent
in the HDR10+ InfoFrame at the InfoFrame's precision, or not used because the
display takes no HDR10+ or Kodi's own tone mapping maps it to SDR, each with
the setting that has Hades map it by the curve.
